-- C29 example: extended surface network (NODEPROP / BRANPROP) with VFP pipeline and tubing tables.
-- Base reservoir = DEPLETION.DATA (15x15x3, solution-gas drive). Two producers in group PLAT flow through a pipeline
-- (VFPPROD table 2) to the FIELD terminal node held at 300 psi. Every time step the network is solved top-down:
-- p(PLAT) = VFP2(q_PLAT, p_FIELD, WCT, GOR); each producer gets p(PLAT) as its THP limit and its tubing table (VFPPROD 1,
-- WCONPROD item 11) turns that into a BHP limit at the current inflow. As the reservoir depletes and the GOR rises the
-- wells switch from the oil-rate target to the network constraint. Results: Custom plots WTHPN (node pressure =
-- THP limit) and WBHP per well, log "Surface network". OPM Flow runs the same network (NETWORK in RUNSPEC).
-- Tables are synthetic: tubing BHP = THP + 8000 ft x 0.25 psi/ft x (1 - 0.1 GOR) (1 + 0.2 WCT) + 1e-6 q^2,
-- pipeline p_in = p_out + 0.02 q (1 + 0.3 GOR)  (q stb/d, GOR Mscf/stb).
-- Expected (C30 implicit network balance): both wells on their 3000 stb/d target for ~2 years (node PLAT ~453 psi), then a
-- smooth network-limited decline (FOPR ~3970 stb/d at 3.5 y, ~2790 at 5 y, ~1040 at 7 y, ~56 at 10 y; PLAT falls to ~300 psi
-- as the rate drops): FOPT 1.054e7 stb vs 1.40e7 stb for the same deck without NODEPROP / BRANPROP (wells on the 500 psi
-- BHP limit) - the back-pressure of the pipeline costs ~25 % of the recovery, the case for artificial lift / a compressor.
-- (C29 balanced explicitly with the rates of the previous step; for this gassy deck that loop oscillated - wells declared
-- dead, revived, dead again - and "died" at ~6.5 y with FOPT 7.1e6. Fixed in C30: see USER_GUIDE section 7d.)
-- Runs in ~3 s.
-- Lines starting with '-- RESSIM:' carry settings ECLIPSE has no keyword for (ignored by ECLIPSE).

